Introduction to Moral Science: Teaches values, ethics, and character building.
Honesty and Truthfulness: Importance of being honest in all situations.
Respect and Kindness: Treating others with dignity and compassion.
Responsibility and Duty: Fulfilling our roles in family and society.
Courage and Determination: Facing challenges with strength.
Empathy and Understanding: Feeling for others and helping them.
Peace and Harmony: Living together in a peaceful manner.
Gratitude: Being thankful for what we have.
Self-Discipline: Controlling our actions and emotions.
Service to Humanity: Helping those in need and contributing to society.
